{
  "_comment": [
    "WINMOL model registry, schema v2. Loader: plugin_utils/model_registry.py (also accepts legacy v1 flat {name: url}).",
    "Entry ids are stable API: the four classic ids (General, Beech, Spruce, Spruce_Deadwood) are unchanged from v1. Their URLs/filenames were REPOINTED (2026-07-21) from the unchecksummed models-onnx-v1 release to the sha256-pinned, numerically-identical models-v1 conversions of the same Keras weights; a previously downloaded General.onnx etc. is no longer recognized and is re-fetched once.",
    "'file' is the mandatory on-disk filename used by BOTH the QGIS plugin (<plugin>/models/) and the batch CLI (--model-dir); it always equals the URL basename (query-stripped) so files fetched manually (gh release download / browser) are recognized.",
    "'sha256' (zoo assets) or 'md5' (Zenodo hdf5) enables integrity verification. EVERY downloadable entry is pinned: tests/test_model_registry.py::test_every_entry_has_a_digest fails the build if an unpinned entry is added.",
    "'preload' lists entry ids installer.download_models may fetch at env-setup time; it ships EMPTY: all downloads are on-demand at selection time.",
    "'recommended' is the ranked default list (best first). recommended[0] MUST equal gui_default. The EFFECTIVE default is device-aware: Registry.default_entry(device) keeps recommended[0]'s FAMILY (the domain choice) and swaps in that family's cpu (int8) or gpu (fp16) variant. Any explicit user/CLI selection overrides it.",
    "'lossless' on a variant means numerically equivalent to its family's fp32 reference; auto variant selection only substitutes a device variant when it is lossless, otherwise it stays on the family default (results-stable).",
    "'hidden': true keeps an entry out of the GUI dropdown (hdf5 originals need TensorFlow; the plugin venv is ONNX-only). They remain addressable by id from the CLI and scripts/convert_models_to_onnx.py.",
    "'Custom' is a reserved id (GUI escape hatch); the loader rejects a registry that defines it.",
    "2026-07-21 ASSET RENAME: every models-v1 release asset was renamed to the consistent scheme model_<Arch>_<Flavour>_512[_<upstream timestamp>][_<qualifier>][_fp16|_int8].onnx, which broke all 22 URLs (HTTP 404, shipped in v0.0.0-demo3). file/url were re-derived from the release SHA256SUMS by sha256 (the bytes are unchanged, so every digest here is untouched). tests/fixtures/models_v1_SHA256SUMS vendors that ground truth and tests/test_model_urls.py guards both the offline file==basename(url) invariant and (with WINMOL_NET_TESTS=1) anonymous reachability."
  ],
